      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Alverton became a coal and coke center when the Donnelly and Mayfield mines opened in 1878.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alverton%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1890s Alverton hosted five coke works, with Mayfield running 104 ovens and Donnelly 254.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alverton%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Southwest Branch of the Pennsylvania Railroad connected Alverton to Greensburg, turning the town into a regional industrial hub.",
